</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1805652Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1805652Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;span.text1805652Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#0000ff; font-weight:bold; text-decoration:underline;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805652Font1&quot;  &gt;This section summarizes the injection procedure for XIAFLEX. HCPs should administer XIAFLEX in their offices, and they must have completed their REMS training and be REMS certified before injecting XIAFLEX. Injection of XIAFLEX into collagen-containing structures such as the corpora cavernosa of the penis may result in damage to those structures, as well as possible injury such as corporal rupture (penile fracture). Therefore, XIAFLEX should be injected only into the Peyronie&apos;s plaque, and care should be taken to avoid injecting into the urethra, nerves, blood vessels, corpora cavernosa, or other collagen-containing structures of the penis. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805652Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805652Font2&quot;  &gt;Please view this video clip on treatment injection &lt;/span &gt;&lt;a href=&quot;##Action 1837218&quot;  &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805652Font3&quot;  &gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805652Font2&quot;  &gt;. &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805652Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf3\cb1\ulc3 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf3\cb1\ulc3\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f2\cf3\cb1\ulc3 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql This section summarizes the injection procedure for XIAFLEX. HCPs should administer XIAFLEX in their offices, and they must have completed their REMS training and be REMS certified before injecting XIAFLEX. Injection of XIAFLEX &#x0A;into collagen-containing structures such as the corpora cavernosa of the penis may result in damage to those structures, as well as possible injury such as corporal rupture (penile fracture). Therefore, XIAFLEX should be injected only into the Peyronie&apos;s &#x0A;plaque, and care should be taken to avoid injecting into the urethra, nerves, blood vessels, corpora cavernosa, or other collagen-containing structures of the penis. \par\par\b Please view this video clip on treatment injection {\field\fldlock{\*\fldinst &#x0A;MERGEFIELD \lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\sshlink\ul  HYPERLINK &quot;##Action 1837218&quot; }{\fldrslt\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\sshlink\ul here}}. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿This section summarizes the injection procedure for XIAFLEX. HCPs should administer XIAFLEX in their offices, and they must have completed their REMS training and be REMS certified before injecting XIAFLEX. Injection of XIAFLEX into collagen-containing structures such as the corpora cavernosa of the penis may result in damage to those structures, as well as possible injury such as corporal rupture (penile fracture). Therefore, XIAFLEX should be injected only into the Peyronie&apos;s plaque, and care should be taken to avoid injecting into the urethra, nerves, blood vessels, corpora cavernosa, or other collagen-containing structures of the penis. &#x0A;Please view this video clip on treatment injection here. &#x0A;</raw>
<numoflines>11</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
