<x>212</x>
<y>241</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>623</cx>
<cy>266</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1817670Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:normal;}&#x0A;li.text1817670Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:normal;}&#x0A;&lt;ol  start=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;list-style-position:outside;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;The reconstituted XIAFLEX solution should be clear. If particulate matter, cloudiness, or discoloration is observed, the solution should not be injected. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;Prior to injection, antiseptic should be applied to the injection site. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;A suitable local anesthetic may be applied, if preferred. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;Withdraw 0.25 mL of reconstituted XIAFLEX into a new, hubless syringe with 0.01-mL graduations with a permanently fixed 27-gauge Â½-inch needle (not supplied). &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;For injection, with the penis in a flaccid state, the needle is placed along the side of the target plaque at the point of maximal concavity. With the needle oriented to enter the edge of the plaque, the needle tip is advanced into the plaque from the side, taking care not to penetrate the tissue under the plaque or perpendicular to the corpora cavernosum. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;Upon plaque entry, the needle is advanced transversely through the width of the plaque toward the other side without exiting the plaque. Proper positioning can be confirmed by resistance to careful minimal plunger depression. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;When the needle is in place, injection can be initiated with the application of measured, consistent pressure while slowly withdrawing the needle; the entire dose should be deposited before the needle is completely removed from the plaque. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;After complete needle withdrawal, pressure should be applied and the injection site dressed appropriately. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;Any unused solution and/or diluent should be discarded. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1817670Font1&quot;  &gt;The second dose of each treatment cycle should be administered 2 to 3 mm from the initial injection site. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/ol &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \froman \fcharset2 Symbol;}{\f3 \fnil \fcharset2 Wingdings;}{\f4 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf2\cb1\ulc2\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f4\cf2\cb1\ulc2 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;{\*\listtable&#x0A;{\list\listtemplateid1&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc4\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;00.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;01.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc1\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;02.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc2\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;03.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc3\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;04.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc4\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;05.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;06.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc1\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;07.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc2\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;08.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listname DefaultList;}\listid1768492093&#x0A;}&#x0A;}&#x0A;{\*\listoverridetable&#x0A;{\listoverride\listid1768492093\listoverridecount0\ls1}&#x0A;}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\pard\s0{\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs24 a.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnstart1\pndec\ls1\ilvl0\pnhang{\pntxta \&apos;2e}}\ls1\ilvl0\fi-450\li450\ql The reconstituted XIAFLEX solution should be clear. If particulate matter, cloudiness, or discoloration &#x0A;is observed, the solution should not be injected. \par\sb120 Prior to injection, antiseptic should be applied to the injection site. \par A suitable local anesthetic may be applied, if preferred. \par Withdraw 0.25 mL of reconstituted XIAFLEX into a new, &#x0A;hubless syringe with 0.01-mL graduations with a permanently fixed 27-gauge \&apos;bd-inch needle (not supplied).  \par For injection, with the penis in a flaccid state, the needle is placed along the side of the target plaque at the point of maximal concavity. &#x0A;With the needle oriented to enter the edge of the plaque, the needle tip is advanced into the plaque from the side, taking care not to penetrate the tissue under the plaque or perpendicular to the corpora cavernosum. \par Upon plaque entry, the needle &#x0A;is advanced transversely through the width of the plaque toward the other side without exiting the plaque. Proper positioning can be confirmed by resistance to careful minimal plunger depression. \par When the needle is in place, injection can be initiated &#x0A;with the application of measured, consistent pressure while slowly withdrawing the needle; the entire dose should be deposited before the needle is completely removed from the plaque. \par After complete needle withdrawal, pressure should be applied and &#x0A;the injection site dressed appropriately. \par Any unused solution and/or diluent should be discarded.  \par The second dose of each treatment cycle should be administered 2 to 3 mm from the initial injection site. \par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿The reconstituted XIAFLEX solution should be clear. If particulate matter, cloudiness, or discoloration is observed, the solution should not be injected. &#x0A;Prior to injection, antiseptic should be applied to the injection site. &#x0A;A suitable local anesthetic may be applied, if preferred. &#x0A;Withdraw 0.25 mL of reconstituted XIAFLEX into a new, hubless syringe with 0.01-mL graduations with a permanently fixed 27-gauge ½-inch needle (not supplied).  &#x0A;For injection, with the penis in a flaccid state, the needle is placed along the side of the target plaque at the point of maximal concavity. With the needle oriented to enter the edge of the plaque, the needle tip is advanced into the plaque from the side, taking care not to penetrate the tissue under the plaque or perpendicular to the corpora cavernosum. &#x0A;Upon plaque entry, the needle is advanced transversely through the width of the plaque toward the other side without exiting the plaque. Proper positioning can be confirmed by resistance to careful minimal plunger depression. &#x0A;When the needle is in place, injection can be initiated with the application of measured, consistent pressure while slowly withdrawing the needle; the entire dose should be deposited before the needle is completely removed from the plaque. &#x0A;After complete needle withdrawal, pressure should be applied and the injection site dressed appropriately. &#x0A;Any unused solution and/or diluent should be discarded.  &#x0A;The second dose of each treatment cycle should be administered 2 to 3 mm from the initial injection site. </raw>
