</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1805621Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1805621Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-style:italic;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805621Font1&quot;  &gt;Prior to administering XIAFLEX, and as part of every treatment-related visit, HCPs must use the patient counseling tool, &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805621Font2&quot;  &gt;What You Need to Know About XIAFLEX Treatment for Peyronie&apos;s Disease: A Patient Guide&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805621Font1&quot;  &gt;, to discuss important information with each patient. Patients should be given this counseling tool to take home for reference, along with a Medication Guide. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf2\cb1\ulc2\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f2\cf2\cb1\ulc2 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 Prior to administering XIAFLEX, and as part of every treatment-related visit, HCPs must use the patient counseling tool, \i What You Need to Know About XIAFLEX Treatment for Peyronie&apos;s Disease: A Patient &#x0A;Guide\i0 , to discuss important information with each patient. Patients should be given this counseling tool to take home for reference, along with a Medication Guide. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Prior to administering XIAFLEX, and as part of every treatment-related visit, HCPs must use the patient counseling tool, What You Need to Know About XIAFLEX Treatment for Peyronie&apos;s Disease: A Patient Guide, to discuss important information with each patient. Patients should be given this counseling tool to take home for reference, along with a Medication Guide. </raw>
<numoflines>5</numoflines>
