</respprops>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>213</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>608</cx>
<cy>271</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1805818Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1805818Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font1&quot;  &gt;XIAFLEX is contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to XIAFLEX or to collagenase used in any other therapeutic application or application method. XIAFLEX is also contraindicated for use in treatment of Peyronie&apos;s disease plaques that involve the penile urethra due to potential risk to this structure. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font1&quot;  &gt;As described in &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font2&quot;  &gt;Section 5.4&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font1&quot;  &gt;, in the Peyronie&apos;s disease trials (Study 1 and Study 2), a greater proportion of XIAFLEX-treated patients (4%) compared to placebo-treated patients (1%) had localized pruritus after up to 4 treatment cycles (involving up to 8 XIAFLEX injection procedures and 4 penile modeling procedures). The incidence of XIAFLEX-associated pruritus was similar after each injection regardless of the number of injections administered. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1805818Font1&quot;  &gt;Because XIAFLEX contains foreign proteins, severe allergic reactions to XIAFLEX can occur. Anaphylaxis has been reported in clinical trials for the other indication for XIAFLEX, Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql XIAFLEX is contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to XIAFLEX or to collagenase used in any other therapeutic application or application method. XIAFLEX is also contraindicated for use in treatment of Peyronie&apos;s &#x0A;disease plaques that involve the penile urethra due to potential risk to this structure. \par\par As described in \b Section 5.4\plain\f1\fs24 , in the Peyronie&apos;s disease trials (Study 1 and Study 2), a greater proportion of XIAFLEX-treated patients (4%) &#x0A;compared to placebo-treated patients (1%) had localized pruritus after up to 4 treatment cycles (involving up to 8 XIAFLEX injection procedures and 4 penile modeling procedures). The incidence of XIAFLEX-associated pruritus was similar after each injection &#x0A;regardless of the number of injections administered. \par\par Because XIAFLEX contains foreign proteins, severe allergic reactions to XIAFLEX can occur. Anaphylaxis has been reported in\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1  clinical trials for the other indication &#x0A;for XIAFLEX, Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿XIAFLEX is contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to XIAFLEX or to collagenase used in any other therapeutic application or application method. XIAFLEX is also contraindicated for use in treatment of Peyronie&apos;s disease plaques that involve the penile urethra due to potential risk to this structure. &#x0A;&#x0A;As described in Section 5.4, in the Peyronie&apos;s disease trials (Study 1 and Study 2), a greater proportion of XIAFLEX-treated patients (4%) compared to placebo-treated patients (1%) had localized pruritus after up to 4 treatment cycles (involving up to 8 XIAFLEX injection procedures and 4 penile modeling procedures). The incidence of XIAFLEX-associated pruritus was similar after each injection regardless of the number of injections administered. &#x0A;&#x0A;Because XIAFLEX contains foreign proteins, severe allergic reactions to XIAFLEX can occur. Anaphylaxis has been reported in clinical trials for the other indication for XIAFLEX, Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. </raw>
<numoflines>15</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
