<x>212</x>
<y>213</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>605</cx>
<cy>127</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1806904Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1806904Font1&quot;  &gt;This section includes a Warning and Precaution concerning the potential for syncope and presyncope based on postmarketing experience. Most syncopal events in patients with Peyronie&apos;s disease treated with XIAFLEX occurred in association with post-injection penile pain and hematoma, penile pain with spontaneous erections, and pain during micturition, suggesting a vasovagal mechanism. If presyncopal symptoms occur, patients should remain recumbent until symptoms resolve, as syncope may be associated with bodily injuries. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 This section includes a Warning and Precaution concerning the potential for syncope and presyncope based on postmarketing experience. Most syncopal events in patients with Peyronie&apos;s disease treated with &#x0A;XIAFLEX occurred in association with post-injection penile pain and hematoma, penile pain with spontaneous erections, and pain during micturition, suggesting a vasovagal mechanism. If presyncopal symptoms occur, patients should remain recumbent until &#x0A;symptoms resolve, as syncope may be associated with bodily injuries. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿This section includes a Warning and Precaution concerning the potential for syncope and presyncope based on postmarketing experience. Most syncopal events in patients with Peyronie&apos;s disease treated with XIAFLEX occurred in association with post-injection penile pain and hematoma, penile pain with spontaneous erections, and pain during micturition, suggesting a vasovagal mechanism. If presyncopal symptoms occur, patients should remain recumbent until symptoms resolve, as syncope may be associated with bodily injuries. </raw>
<numoflines>7</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
