<x>212</x>
<y>213</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>603</cx>
<cy>163</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1807385Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807385Font1&quot;  &gt;The safety of XIAFLEX in treatment of Peyronie&apos;s disease was assessed in 2 identical phase 3 placebo-controlled clinical trials. Adverse event data from the 2 pivotal trials were pooled and included 832 patients; 551 received XIAFLEX and 281 received placebo. 92% of patients in the XIAFLEX group experienced at least 1 adverse reaction as compared to 61% of those in the placebo group. Most adverse reactions were local events of the penis and groin; the majority of the events were mild or moderate in severity, and most (79%) resolved within 14 days of the XIAFLEX injection. The adverse reaction profile was similar after each injection, regardless of the number of injections administered. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 The safety of XIAFLEX in treatment of Peyronie&apos;s disease was assessed in 2 identical phase 3 placebo-controlled clinical trials. Adverse event data from the 2 pivotal trials were pooled and included 832 &#x0A;patients; 551 received XIAFLEX and 281 received placebo. 92% of patients in the XIAFLEX group experienced at least 1 adverse reaction as compared to 61% of those in the placebo group. Most adverse reactions were local events of the penis and groin; the &#x0A;majority of the events were mild or moderate in severity, and most (79%) resolved within 14 days of the XIAFLEX injection. The adverse reaction profile was similar after each injection, regardless of the number of injections administered. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿The safety of XIAFLEX in treatment of Peyronie&apos;s disease was assessed in 2 identical phase 3 placebo-controlled clinical trials. Adverse event data from the 2 pivotal trials were pooled and included 832 patients; 551 received XIAFLEX and 281 received placebo. 92% of patients in the XIAFLEX group experienced at least 1 adverse reaction as compared to 61% of those in the placebo group. Most adverse reactions were local events of the penis and groin; the majority of the events were mild or moderate in severity, and most (79%) resolved within 14 days of the XIAFLEX injection. The adverse reaction profile was similar after each injection, regardless of the number of injections administered. </raw>
<numoflines>9</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
