<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1807354Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1807354Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Symbol&quot;, serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807354Font1&quot;  &gt;In clinical trials (Study 1 and Study 2), the most frequently reported adverse drug reactions (&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807354Font2&quot;  &gt;Â³&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807354Font1&quot;  &gt;25%) of patients treated with XIAFLEX and at an incidence greater than placebo were penile hematoma, penile swelling, and penile pain. The incidence of adverse events in the clinical trials is shown in Table 5. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \froman \fcharset2 Symbol;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}{\cs3\cf0\cb1\ulc0 normaltextrun;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql In clinical trials (Study 1 and Study 2), the most frequently reported adverse drug reactions (\lang1033\hich\f2\loch\f2 \&apos;b3\plain\f1\fs24 25%) of patients treated with XIAFLEX and at an incidence greater than placebo were penile &#x0A;hematoma, penile swelling, and penile pain. The incidence of adverse events in the clinical trials is shown in Table 5. \par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿In clinical trials (Study 1 and Study 2), the most frequently reported adverse drug reactions (³25%) of patients treated with XIAFLEX and at an incidence greater than placebo were penile hematoma, penile swelling, and penile pain. The incidence of adverse events in the clinical trials is shown in Table 5. </raw>
