<text id="1808927" parent="1808921" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" defaulttext="none" verticalscroll="true">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769113798</lastupdated>
<respprops>
<tabletportrait>
<text>
<possize>
<size>
<cx>478</cx>
<cy>159</cy>
</size>
</possize>
</text>
</tabletportrait>
</respprops>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>213</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>613</cx>
<cy>253</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1808927Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1808927Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot;  &gt;This section gives additional data on acute lower back pain reactions observed during postapproval use of XIAFLEX during retreatment injections. It is noted that, because these reactions are reported voluntarily from a population of uncertain size, it is not always possible to reliably estimate their frequency. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot;  &gt;In addition to the pain described in &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font2&quot;  &gt;Section 5.6&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot;  &gt;, some patients have also experienced temporary gait instability and an inability to walk for brief periods of time post-injection. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot;  &gt;This section also notes reports of localized skin and soft tissue necrosis occurring after penile hematoma, some of which required surgical intervention. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808927Font1&quot;  &gt;Additionally, the section reiterates that syncopal and presyncopal events have been reported in patients treated with XIAFLEX postapproval. Most of these cases occurred in the immediate treatment period or within 1 to 2 days following injection. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 This section gives additional data on acute lower back pain reactions observed during postapproval use of XIAFLEX during retreatment injections. It is noted that, because these reactions are reported voluntarily &#x0A;from a population of uncertain size, it is not always possible to reliably estimate their frequency.  \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 In addition to the pain described in \b Section 5.6\b0 , some patients have also experienced temporary &#x0A;gait instability and an inability to walk for brief periods of time post-injection. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 This section also notes reports of localized skin and soft tissue necrosis occurring after penile hematoma, some of which &#x0A;required surgical intervention. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 Additionally, the section reiterates that syncopal and presyncopal events have been reported in patients treated with XIAFLEX postapproval. Most of these cases occurred in &#x0A;the immediate treatment period or within 1 to 2 days following injection. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿This section gives additional data on acute lower back pain reactions observed during postapproval use of XIAFLEX during retreatment injections. It is noted that, because these reactions are reported voluntarily from a population of uncertain size, it is not always possible to reliably estimate their frequency.  &#x0A;In addition to the pain described in Section 5.6, some patients have also experienced temporary gait instability and an inability to walk for brief periods of time post-injection. &#x0A;This section also notes reports of localized skin and soft tissue necrosis occurring after penile hematoma, some of which required surgical intervention. &#x0A;Additionally, the section reiterates that syncopal and presyncopal events have been reported in patients treated with XIAFLEX postapproval. Most of these cases occurred in the immediate treatment period or within 1 to 2 days following injection. </raw>
<numoflines>14</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
