<html>span.text1808998Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808998Font1&quot;  &gt;XIAFLEX is the only treatment evaluated in 2 large multi-centered studies of Peyronie&apos;s disease patients. The efficacy of XIAFLEX was assessed in 2 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multi-centered trials in 832 adult males with Peyronie&apos;s disease (Study 1 and Study 2). At study entry, patients must have had penile curvature deformity of at least 30Â° in the stable phase of Peyronie&apos;s disease but no ventral curve deformity, an isolated hourglass deformity, or a calcified plaque; most patients (98%) had only mild or no penile pain. In these trials, patients were given up to 4 treatment cycles of XIAFLEX or placebo (weeks 0, 6, 12, and 18) and were followed in a nontreatment follow-up period (weeks 24â€“52). &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808998Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1808998Font1&quot;  &gt;In each treatment cycle, 2 injections of XIAFLEX or 2 injections of placebo were administered 1 to 3 days apart. A penile modeling procedure was performed 1 to 3 days after the second injection. The treatment cycle was repeated at approximately 6-week intervals for up to 3 additional times for a maximum of 8 total injection procedures and 4 total modeling procedures. Patients also performed at-home penile modeling for 6 weeks. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql XIAFLEX is the only treatment evaluated in 2 large multi-centered studies of Peyronie&apos;s disease patients. The efficacy of XIAFLEX was assessed in 2 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multi-centered trials in 832 adult &#x0A;males with Peyronie&apos;s disease (Study 1 and Study 2). At study entry, patients must have had penile curvature deformity of at least 30\plain\f1\fs24\u176 \&apos;b0\plain\f1\fs24  in the stable phase of Peyronie&apos;s disease but no ventral curve deformity, an isolated &#x0A;hourglass deformity, or a calcified plaque; most patients (98%) had only mild or no penile pain. In these trials, patients were given up to 4 treatment cycles of XIAFLEX or placebo (weeks 0, 6, 12, and 18) and were followed in a nontreatment follow-up &#x0A;period (weeks 24\plain\f1\fs24\u8211 \&apos;96\plain\f1\fs24 52).  \par\par In each treatment cycle, 2 injections of XIAFLEX or 2 injections of placebo were administered 1 to 3 days apart. A penile modeling procedure was performed 1 to 3 days after the second &#x0A;injection. The treatment cycle was repeated at approximately 6-week intervals for up to 3 additional times for a maximum of 8 total injection procedures and 4 total modeling procedures. Patients also performed at-home penile modeling for 6 weeks. \par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿XIAFLEX is the only treatment evaluated in 2 large multi-centered studies of Peyronie&apos;s disease patients. The efficacy of XIAFLEX was assessed in 2 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multi-centered trials in 832 adult males with Peyronie&apos;s disease (Study 1 and Study 2). At study entry, patients must have had penile curvature deformity of at least 30° in the stable phase of Peyronie&apos;s disease but no ventral curve deformity, an isolated hourglass deformity, or a calcified plaque; most patients (98%) had only mild or no penile pain. In these trials, patients were given up to 4 treatment cycles of XIAFLEX or placebo (weeks 0, 6, 12, and 18) and were followed in a nontreatment follow-up period (weeks 24–52).  &#x0A;In each treatment cycle, 2 injections of XIAFLEX or 2 injections of placebo were administered 1 to 3 days apart. A penile modeling procedure was performed 1 to 3 days after the second injection. The treatment cycle was repeated at approximately 6-week intervals for up to 3 additional times for a maximum of 8 total injection procedures and 4 total modeling procedures. Patients also performed at-home penile modeling for 6 weeks. </raw>
