<html>span.text1809560Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1809560Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-style:italic;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809560Font1&quot;  &gt;In both Study 1 and Study 2, there was a significant reduction in the coprimary endpoint of patient-reported Bother scores (âˆ’1.2 and âˆ’1.1, respectively).&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809560Font3&quot;  &gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809560Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809560Font1&quot;  &gt;Table 11 shows the mean change in patient-reported Bother score from baseline to week 52 for Study 1 and Study 2.&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql In both Study 1 and Study 2, there was a significant reduction in the coprimary endpoint of patient-reported Bother scores (\plain\f1\fs24\u8722 \&apos;3f\plain\f1\fs24 1.2 and \plain\f1\fs24\u8722 \&apos;3f\plain\f1\fs24 1.1, respectively).\i &#x0A; \lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\line\plain\f1\fs24\par Table 11 shows the mean change in patient-reported Bother score from baseline to week 52 for Study 1 and Study 2.\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿In both Study 1 and Study 2, there was a significant reduction in the coprimary endpoint of patient-reported Bother scores (−1.2 and −1.1, respectively). &#x0F;&#x0A;Table 11 shows the mean change in patient-reported Bother score from baseline to week 52 for Study 1 and Study 2.</raw>
