<html>span.text1809706Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809706Font1&quot;  &gt;Corresponding to the data in Table 11, Figures 4 and 5 show the mean change in patient-reported Peyronie&apos;s disease Bother domain score during 52 weeks of follow-up in Study 1 and Study 2 for patients treated with placebo (âˆ’2.8 and âˆ’2.6, respectively) and XIAFLEX (âˆ’1.6 and âˆ’1.5, respectively). &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql Corresponding to the data in Table 11, Figures 4 and 5 show the mean change in patient-reported Peyronie&apos;s disease Bother domain score during 52 weeks of follow-up in Study 1 and Study 2 for patients treated with placebo (\plain\f1\fs24\u8722 &#x0A;\&apos;3f\plain\f1\fs24 2.8 and \plain\f1\fs24\u8722 \&apos;3f\plain\f1\fs24 2.6, respectively) and XIAFLEX (\plain\f1\fs24\u8722 \&apos;3f\plain\f1\fs24 1.6 and \plain\f1\fs24\u8722 \&apos;3f\plain\f1\fs24 1.5, respectively). \par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Corresponding to the data in Table 11, Figures 4 and 5 show the mean change in patient-reported Peyronie&apos;s disease Bother domain score during 52 weeks of follow-up in Study 1 and Study 2 for patients treated with placebo (−2.8 and −2.6, respectively) and XIAFLEX (−1.6 and −1.5, respectively). </raw>
