<text id="1809838" parent="1809832" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" defaulttext="none" verticalscroll="true">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769457577</lastupdated>
<respprops>
<tabletportrait>
<text>
<possize>
<size>
<cx>480</cx>
<cy>147</cy>
</size>
</possize>
</text>
</tabletportrait>
</respprops>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>197</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>614</cx>
<cy>219</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1809838Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1809838Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-style:italic;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809838Font1&quot;  &gt;The XIAFLEX PI includes counseling recommendations for HCPs. HCPs should explicitly share all of the information contained within the Patient Counseling Information section of the PI with their patients. Patients should be advised of serious complications of XIAFLEX injection, including corporal rupture, penile hematoma, skin and soft tissue necrosis related to penile hematoma, and these events may require surgery to correct the complication. Patients should also be advised about the risk of transient, self-resolving, mild-to-severe post-injection back pain reactions that may radiate to the legs, chest, and arms, and may include spasms. &lt;br /&gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809838Font1&quot;  &gt;After the injection, patients should be advised of potential bruising, swelling, and/or mild-to-moderate penile pain that can be relieved by taking over-the-counter medication; to call the physician without delay for any severe pain, swelling, or purpling of the penis; difficult urination; blood in the urine; sudden loss of the ability to maintain an erection, especially if accompanied by a popping or cracking sound; to return to their HCP as directed for additional injection(s) or modeling procedure(s); to not have intercourse between the first and second injections of each treatment cycle; to wait 4 weeks after the second injection of a treatment cycle before resuming sexual activity; to perform gentle, at-home modeling activities as recommended; to refrain from using a vacuum erection device during XIAFLEX treatment; and to avoid abdominal straining.&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1809838Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf2\cb1\ulc2\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f2\cf2\cb1\ulc2 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql The XIAFLEX PI includes counseling recommendations for HCPs. HCPs should explicitly share all of the information contained within the Patient Counseling Information section of the PI with their patients. Patients should be advised &#x0A;of serious complications of XIAFLEX injection, including corporal rupture, penile hematoma, skin and soft tissue necrosis related to penile hematoma, and these events may require surgery to correct the complication. Patients should also be advised about &#x0A;the risk of transient, self-resolving, mild-to-severe post-injection back pain reactions that may radiate to the legs, chest, and arms, and may include spasms. \lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\line\plain\f1\fs24\par After the injection, patients should be advised &#x0A;of potential bruising, swelling, and/or mild-to-moderate penile pain that can be relieved by taking over-the-counter medication; to call the physician without delay for any severe pain, swelling, or purpling of the penis; difficult urination; blood in &#x0A;the urine; sudden loss of the ability to maintain an erection, especially if accompanied by a popping or cracking sound; to return to their HCP as directed for additional injection(s) or modeling procedure(s); to not have intercourse between the first &#x0A;and second injections of each treatment cycle; to wait 4 weeks after the second injection of a treatment cycle before resuming sexual activity; to perform gentle, at-home modeling activities as recommended; to refrain from using a vacuum erection device &#x0A;during XIAFLEX treatment; and to avoid abdominal straining.\i\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿The XIAFLEX PI includes counseling recommendations for HCPs. HCPs should explicitly share all of the information contained within the Patient Counseling Information section of the PI with their patients. Patients should be advised of serious complications of XIAFLEX injection, including corporal rupture, penile hematoma, skin and soft tissue necrosis related to penile hematoma, and these events may require surgery to correct the complication. Patients should also be advised about the risk of transient, self-resolving, mild-to-severe post-injection back pain reactions that may radiate to the legs, chest, and arms, and may include spasms. &#x0F;&#x0A;After the injection, patients should be advised of potential bruising, swelling, and/or mild-to-moderate penile pain that can be relieved by taking over-the-counter medication; to call the physician without delay for any severe pain, swelling, or purpling of the penis; difficult urination; blood in the urine; sudden loss of the ability to maintain an erection, especially if accompanied by a popping or cracking sound; to return to their HCP as directed for additional injection(s) or modeling procedure(s); to not have intercourse between the first and second injections of each treatment cycle; to wait 4 weeks after the second injection of a treatment cycle before resuming sexual activity; to perform gentle, at-home modeling activities as recommended; to refrain from using a vacuum erection device during XIAFLEX treatment; and to avoid abdominal straining.</raw>
<numoflines>19</numoflines>
